# Normalize line endings.
# Repo blobs are stored as LF; the eol attribute controls what gets
# checked out on disk. This project is developed on Windows/Visual Studio,
# so text files check out as CRLF by default.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Shell scripts are run through bash on Linux/macOS. A CRLF before a
# line-continuation backslash breaks the continuation (bash sees a
# literal \r), so these must stay LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch line endings.
*.jpg -text
*.ttf -text
*.png -text
*.ico -text
